Here's a conceptual design for the UPayU Bridge (Sip Drip) integration with the RUHBI Payroll System, combining a playful 8-bit game mechanic with real-world payroll functionality. This will use the integrations with Mission, Acorn Tap, and Morbraii to create a gamified engagement layer.
1. System Overview: UPayU Bridge (Sip Drip)
Core Idea:
A browser-based 8-bit game ("Sip Drip") where users earn points by clicking to "sip" (small rewards) or "drip" (larger rewards). Points accumulate in the RUHBI Payroll System, unlocking real-world benefits (e.g., bonuses, discounts, or mission-based tasks).
Key Integrations:
Mission: Task-based rewards (e.g., "Complete 5 tasks → 100 points").
Acorn Tap: Micro-savings integration (e.g., "Sip 10 points → $1 deposit").
Morbraii: Identity verification/onboarding (e.g., "Drip 50 points → Unlock premium features").
2. Technical Architecture
Frontend (Sip Drip Game)
Game Mechanics:
Sip: Click to earn small points (e.g., 1-5 points).
Drip: Hold/long-click to earn larger points (e.g., 10-20 points).
Visuals: 8-bit pixel art (e.g., retro UI, animated droplets).
Sound: Chiptune audio (e.g., 8-bit "sip/drip" sounds).
UI Components:
html
⌄
<!-- Example Sip/Drip UI -->
<div class="game-container">
<div class="sip-button" onclick="sipPoints()">SIP</div>
<div class="drip-button" ondblclick="dripPoints()">DRIP</div>
<div class="points-display">Points: <span id="points">0</span></div>
<div class="rewards">
<p>100 pts → $1 (Acorn Tap)</p>
<p>50 pts → Unlock Mission</p>
</div>
</div>
Backend (UPayU Bridge API)
Endpoints:
POST /api/sip → Increment points by 1-5.
POST /api/drip → Increment points by 10-20 (with cooldown).
GET /api/balance → Fetch user’s total points.
POST /api/convert → Exchange points for rewards (e.g., $1 → 100 pts).
